y\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 iv  staff  26860 Sep 17 23:43 rework_test.go\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 iv  staff  17116 Sep 17 23:31 run_test.go\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 iv  staff  13436 Sep 17 23:25 run.go\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 iv  staff    664 Sep 17 20:17 sync.go\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 iv  staff  28638 Sep 17 23:42 TRACEABILITY.md\\n===\\ndiff --git a/LOGBOOK.md b/LOGBOOK.md\\nindex 43c6d21..d57be37 100644\\n--- a/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n@@ -5,6 +5,23 @@\\n \\n ## 2026-09-17\\n \\n+### TASK-260830-1geqhj rev2 — ax pane rework: authority, window, closure, realm\\n+- REWORKED on `888ae3d` after review-verdict-rev1 (18 findings): event authority through `fencing.AuthorizeMutation` with local-hold-only emission and the §5.7 fold gate (`sessstate.Reduce`); realm authorization through the admitted `credential_capable_execution_realm` row bound to host binding/build/generation (bare boolean removed); bootstrap window closed by the winner's `HasCheckpoint` with atomic `Supersede`; checkpoint admission bound to the winning lease and session; profile from the checkpoint closure (`DeriveForHeads`); journal source bound to the lease checkpoint; non-interactive `headless_creation` conditional; remote non-interactive parks per §4.2 step 5.\\n+- F1: a park decision's stale/unverified presented token never authors — `Emit` presents the winning tuple itself, so verified local-winner parks (stale, material, checkpoint) emit while remote/unverified/ambiguous/handoff parks refuse; `Run` pre-checks local hold + foldability and parks without evidence rather than manufacturing a §5.2 collision.\\n+- F2: the bootstrap window is the winner's `HasCheckpoint`, not a clock: in-window changed ops refuse `idempotency_mismatch` in both modes, post-window new ops supersede via staged rename; the `binding-*.tmp` sweep is age-gated (1 min) so a concurrent live stage is never deleted.\\n+- F3: resume profile is the checkpoint closure, not the head: `Run` loads the winner's heads even when the checkpoint is not otherwise required, so a head-only or losing-lease `profile.changed` never drives launch (§2.4, §13.10).\\n+- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 35 narrowing mutants, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 36/36 with control); reviewer's RM1/RM2/RM4 survivors now killed by `TestRunTornLeasePropagates`, `TestDecideRemoteOwnerPrecedesMaterialization`, `TestDecideRestoreChangedOperationRefuses`. AC 41/41 re-derived with the six previously unfaithful rows re-pinned.\\n+- Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n+\\n+### TASK-260830-1geqhj — ax pane enforcement wrapper validation core (first leaf)\\n+- DELIVERED: `internal/axpane` — the pure `Decide` core (`launch|reattach|attach_remote|takeover_offer|parked|refused`), the `Run` orchestration over real stores, the durable bootstrap `(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)` binding store, §5.2 event authorship, and the §7.A descriptor builder. Every check composes a landed gate (`fencing`, `matjournal`, `sessckpt`/`sessrepo`, `sessprofile`, `provhost`, `resumesmoke`, `terminalbackend`, `config`, `axerror`); nothing is re-implemented. First leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe; `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract (final leaf re-pins).\\n+- F1: `fencing` launch entries refuse — not park — foreign sessions, malformed tokens, and lapsed grants, so the wrapper's `refused(lease_conflict)` rows for foreign/expired inputs compose directly; only remote/ambiguous/unverified/absent/stale ownership parks. Remote parks resolve locally to `attach_remote` (interactive + attach admitted) or `takeover_offer`, and both offers still author `session.parked` with `remote_owner`.\\n+- F2: the tuple gate must precede profile mapping in arm order: `ResolveMapping` re-checks the tuple internally, so mapping-first would wear tuple refusals as `profile_mapping_unavailable`. The standalone `CheckResumeTuple` call stays as fail-fast ordering; weakening it alone is unobservable (defense in depth, stated in TRACEABILITY.md).\\n+- F3: `terminalbackend.Reconcile` maps generation drift to the more specific `terminal_backend_stale_generation` (not the generic mismatch), and `create` is conferred by both `durable_disconnect` and `headless_creation` — the unproven vector must deny both. `sessckpt.Get` re-attests through `sessrepo` on every read, so checkpoint admission composes through the read path.\\n+- F4: `Bind` is linearizable on the commit race via link-EEXIST re-read (same operation reattaches to the winner, changed operation refuses); the `AfterStage` hook plays the concurrent winner deterministically in tests. The store stamps `created_at` itself — scalar timestamps require ≥3 fractional digits, so `time.RFC3339Nano` (which omits trailing zeros) is not a valid stamp.\\n+- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 24 narrowing mutants, all KILLED by named tests through `internal/axpane/mutant_harness.py`, plus the applied harmless SURVIVED control (25/25 rows match; per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits in the outcome tar). No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text.\\n+- AC: 41 of 41 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md`); crash/idempotency evidence via the no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-kill pattern. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n+\\n ### TASK-260830-2x16gz — hostile-network conformance suite + AC-HOST-001 (final leaf)\\n - DELIVERED: `internal/hostchannel/hostile_test.go` + `hostile_carrier_test.go` re-derive all seven story cases through the real `Dial`/`Serve`/`Call` entries with per-vector Section 15 classes and state censuses, and execute the AC-HOST-001 rows: real OpenSSH loopback carrier (unprivileged `sshd`, forced command, exact `ServeArgv` on the wire, TLS-first bytes, no PTY, bounded stderr), rotation/enrollment lifecycle, copied-key halves, revocation fencing, stale-read integrity, recovery bypasses, concurrency/stall races, role swap, and the v4 loader gate. Test-only leaf; no production file changed. P3 notes closed (`ax-host/2` vector, bad-destination deadline hook).\\n - F1: when the SERVER refuses mid-handshake, production `Dial` stably reports `transport_failure` (alert/close rendezvous; TLS 1.3 lets the client finish first) while `Serve` deterministically reports `authentication_failed`; only the initiator's OWN verification failure surfaces as `authentication_failed` on `Dial`. Tests pin both sides; the rendezvous resolves at the hello bound.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 7477,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1870,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
