{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c64f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b131-d4f6-7b82-a7a6-5363cf3ac7fb"},"sequence":386,"recorded_at":1780531400000767,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"2237b1e3-856b-4a22-9f46-61adba667efd","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"2237b1e3-856b-4a22-9f46-61adba667efd","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"2237b1e3-856b-4a22-9f46-61adba667efd"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b132-c84c-7700-88cf-2e0c6b332747"},"task_id":"01a0b132-c84c-7700-88cf-2e0c6b332747","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b132-c84c-7700-88cf-2e0c6b332747","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/TASK-260830-1geqhj/review-rev2/TASK-260830-1geqhj_review-verdict-rev2.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-1geqhj — independent review verdict, CR-TASK-260830-1geqhj-2 revision 2\n2|\n3|**Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED (routed `to-dev`).** One P1 class, two P2, eight P3.\n4|\n5|Reviewer: RUN-260917-368f1f (claude-opus-5 max). Reviewed bytes: base\n6|`888ae3dff6a55c29bfaf311957748d405ed1ab06`, candidate tree\n7|`0a5c5e7818aa94404420a4f2904924fc90e76083` (recomputed from the live Story\n8|worktree with an untracked-aware temporary index: equal), patch sha256\n9|`3a6ab390af68440df8791d3949378ffb2dfd3627010aa24b693d8a34faec31ff` (equal to\n10|the CR record). Every probe ran in an isolated `git archive` copy of the exact\n11|candidate tree under `.temp/TASK-260830-1geqhj/review-rev2/cand/`; the live\n12|Story worktree, index, branch and HEAD were never touched. Every instrument,\n13|raw log and subprocess exit is in\n14|`TASK-260830-1geqhj_review-evidence-rev2.tar.gz` (paths below are relative to\n15|that archive). `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` everywhere; 0 `__pycache__` left.\n16|\n17|## Rework verification — the twelve rev1 findings, graded on my own executed evidence\n18|\n19|A finding is \"fixed\" only when the reported vector refuses AND a vector one\n20|step away refuses. Probe names are the tests in\n21|`probes/zz_review2_probe_test.go` (`logs/10-review-probes.log`,\n22|`logs/11-review-probes-b.log`); mutant rows are in `review2_mutants.py`\n23|(`logs/50-*`, `logs/51-*`, raw per-plant logs in `logs/mutants-pass{1,2}/`).\n24|\n25|| rev1 finding | Grade | Executed evidence |\n26|| --- | --- | --- |\n27|| P1-1 `session.parked` authored under a remote-held lease; no `AuthorizeMutation` caller; unfoldable lifecycle event | **Fixed** | `TestR2ProbeRemoteOwnerParkNoRemoteLeaseEvent`: remote winner → `parked(remote_owner)` / `attach_remote`, `Emitted=false`, event count 1→1, and the owner's own `(B, seq 1)` event then appends cleanly (the rev1 collision is gone). `TestR2ProbeUnverifiedRemoteHolderNoEvent`: unverified+remote → no event. `TestR2ProbeParkedFoldsInStateEngine`: creating chain parks with no emission and `sessstate.Reduce` folds `creating`. `TestR2ProbeLosingLeaseReachesMutationGate` (foldable `failed` chain): losing `(1,A)` under remote `(2,B)` → `not_owner`; under local successor `(2,A2)` → `stale_owner` — the mutation gate itself refuses, not the fold pre-check. `TestN2ProbeStaleLocalPresentedSameEpoch`: a losing same-epoch presented lease under the held local winner parks `stale_owner` and authors under lease A (the held winner) at seq 3; the chain folds to `parked` after one park and after a second one. `TestR2ProbeLosingLeaseProfileEventIgnored` (probe 15): losing-lease `profile.changed` never becomes the launch pair (`standard`, no source). Residual: P3-1 below (the losing-epoch arm of the gate is unpinned by the committed suite). |\n28|| P1-2 bare `AttestedServer` boolean; smoke unbound to generation/OS | **Fixed** (background path) | `TestR2ProbeBackgroundCachedSmokeNeverAuthorizes`: background + cached passing smoke, no realm row → `refused capability_unavailable`; smoke not required, no row → `capability_unavailable`; admitted row + stale typed generation → `capability_unavailable`; admitted row + smoke target bound to a stale generation → `target_auth_missing`; admitted row expired at the admission instant → refused (`terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch at evidence liveness`); pre-reboot row after the raw generation moved → refused (`terminal_backend_stale_generation`). Mutant RV1 (cross-bind verdict ignored) KILLED ×2 by `TestDecideRealmBindingMismatchRefuses`. The boolean no longer exists as an input (`Realm` has no such member; `grep AttestedServer` = 0). Residuals: P3-4 (foreground credential path), P3-5 (evidence order), P3-6 (expired-row refusal class). |\n29|| P1-3 bootstrap window never closes; RM4 survived | **Fixed only for successor leases → P1-1** | `TestR2ProbePostWindowRestoreWithSourcedJournal`: after a local successor lease carrying the captured checkpoint, restore with a NEW operation and a journal sourced from that checkpoint → `launch`, binding = op2 (the producer's own `TestRunPostWindowSupersedes` drops the materialization requirement; this probe keeps it). In a fresh world (winner without checkpoint) the changed op → `refused idempotency_mismatch`. `TestN2ProbeWindowVsRemoteOwner`: a remote winner that closed the window + changed local op → `parked(remote_owner)`, not a mismatch. Mutants RV4 (window closes on any winner) KILLED ×2 by `TestDecideRestoreChangedOperationRefuses`/`TestDecideTable`/`TestRunIdempotencyMismatch`; RV6 (= reviewer RM4, idempotency arm skipped in restore mode) KILLED ×2 by `TestDecideRestoreChangedOperationRefuses`. **But** the window predicate reads `Winner.HasCheckpoint`, a lease-record fact that is null for every epoch-1 owner forever (see P1-1): `TestN2ProbeEpochOneOwnerAfterCheckpoint` — same-host session stopped with a published checkpoint (landed engine: `state=stopped HasCheckpoint=true newest=C`; lease: `epoch=1 HasCheckpoint=false`), restore with a new operation → **`refused idempotency_mismatch` \"inside the bootstrap window\"** — the rev1 P1-3 symptom on the creating host, unless a takeover happened. Residuals: **P1-1**, **P2-1** (supersession destroys the prior pair's receipt), P3-2 (create-from-stopped through `Run` unpinned). |\n30|| P1-4 checkpoint admission unbound to lease and session | **Partially fixed → P1-1 below** | Reported vectors refuse: `TestR2ProbeCheckpointAdmissionBound`: caller checkpoint ≠ lease checkpoint → `parked(restore_policy)` \"required checkpoint is not the winning lease checkpoint\"; a foreign-session checkpoint → \"checkpoint names another session\", even when the lease itself names that foreign digest. Mutant RV9 (lease binding narrowed to launch mode) KILLED ×2 by `TestDecideCheckpointNotLeaseParks`. One step away it admits: with a null lease checkpoint (every epoch-1 owner) any attested checkpoint of the session is admitted, including one the chain never published while the chain's newest is another — see P1-1. |\n31|| P2-1 profile from the session head on resume | **Fixed**, with a residual P2 | `TestR2ProbeResumeProfileUsesClosure`: resume from C1 with a head-only `profile.changed` → `standard`, no source (Decide); through `Run` with the winner carrying the checkpoint and an authoritative head-only `profile.changed` under the winner → `standard`, no source, in restore mode and in create-from-stopped. Shipped N-profile-closure KILLED. Residual: **P2-2** (`Run` silently falls back to the session head when no checkpoint store is bound). |\n32|| P2-2 materialization = `Phase == committed` alone | **Fixed** for a checkpoint-bearing winner | `TestR2ProbeMaterializationOneGenerationBehind`: committed journal sourced one generation behind → `parked(restore_policy)` \"sourced from a superseded checkpoint\"; prepared journal sourced from the lease checkpoint → parked; committed + sourced from the lease checkpoint → launch. Shipped N-materialization-source KILLED ×2. With a null lease checkpoint (every epoch-1 owner) the source binding is vacuous — P1-1 below, second vector. |\n33|| P2-3 `headless_creation` never evaluated | **Fixed** | `TestR2ProbeNonInteractiveWithoutHeadless` through `Run`: probed `headless_creation=false`, non-interactive create → `refused terminal_backend_capability_unproven`; the interactive create on the same backend launches. Shipped N-headless KILLED ×2. |\n34|| P2-4 step-5 label | **Fixed** | `TestR2ProbeRemoteOwnerLabels`: non-interactive remote owner → `parked(remote_owner)` in launch and restore mode; interactive + attach admitted → `attach_remote`; interactive + attach unproven → `takeover_offer`. Table row and TRACEABILITY corrected. |\n35|| P2-5 survived reviewer mutants RM1/RM2/RM4 | **Fixed** | RV5 (= RM1, `ObserveOwnership` error swallowed) KILLED ×2 by `TestRunTornLeasePropagates`; RV2 (= RM2, steps 3/4 swapped) KILLED ×2 by `TestDecideRemoteOwnerPrecedesMaterialization`; RV6 (= RM4) KILLED ×2. Deterministic across both passes (`logs/50`, `logs/51`). |\n36|| P3-1 `binding-*.tmp` never swept | **Fixed** | `TestBindSweepsStaleStaging` (age-gated 1 min); my `TestR2ProbeCrashBeforeCommit` shows a fresh pre-commit staging file is retained for the minute by design and the retry still installs exactly one `binding.json`. |\n37|| P3-2 hygiene (duplicate `N-discovery`, `doc.go:29` `AuthorizeInput`, \"nothing re-implemented\") | **Fixed** | TRACEABILITY mutant table = 36 rows, no duplicate name, equal to the 36-row harness; `doc.go` names `AuthorizeMutation` and no `AuthorizeInput` (`grep AuthorizeInput internal/axpane` = 0); `ParkedPayload`/`checkEvidenceIDs` are justified as fail-fast guards. |\n38|| P3-3 landed `fencing.Authorize` ordering / `sessrepo.checkAppend` | Not this leaf's (orchestrator items) | `TestR2ProbeConflictingArmsAndClosedSets`: remote interactive owner + lapsed local grant still refuses `lease_conflict` (landed order); nothing in the candidate touches `fencing`/`sessrepo`. |\n39|\n40|## What holds (verified myself, exact candidate tree)\n41|\n42|| Check | Result | Evidence |\n43|| --- | --- | --- |\n44|| gofmt / go vet / go build; GOOS=linux, GOOS=windows builds; `go vet ./...` | all exit 0 | `logs/01-fmt-vet-build.log`, `logs/70-tree-exact-checks.log` |\n45|| tracecheck (registry untouched: contracts=63 sections=36) / `cataloggen -adopted … -check` | exit 0 / 0 | `logs/70` |\n46|| `go test ./internal/axpane -count=1 -v` | exit 0, 148 PASS lines, 0 FAIL | `logs/05-axpane-test-v.log` |\n47|| axpane+fencing+sessprofile+matjournal+sessckpt+provhost | all ok | `logs/71-six-packages.log` |\n48|| Shipped harness, isolated copy, two full passes with raw per-plant output | 36/36 match both passes (35 KILLED, control SURVIVED); production blobs restored (OIDs equal to the live candidate) | `logs/40`, `logs/41`, `logs/42-post-harness-blob-oids.log` |\n49|| My mutants (whole suite as killer, two passes) | 8 KILLED ×2 (RV1, RV2, RV3 park-reason collapse, RV4, RV5, RV6, RV9, RV10), control SURVIVED ×2; 3 SURVIVED ×2 (RV7, RV8, RV11 — graded below) | `logs/50`, `logs/51`, `logs/mutants-pass{1,2}/*.log`, `logs/53-delta-witness-under-mutants.log` |\n50|| RV8 (Run's remote-holder pre-check dropped) SURVIVED harmlessly | under the mutant the remote park still emits nothing: the composed `AuthorizeMutation` gate refuses `not_owner` — the pre-check is defense in depth and the composition catches the bypass | `logs/53` |\n51|| Real-kill after commit (`TestBindCrashChildSelfTerminates`) + hooks + concurrency, ×2 | PASS ×2 | `logs/60-crash-rerun-x2.log` |\n52|| My real SIGKILL before commit / after commit (Bind) | absence proven then exactly one `binding.json` on retry; the committed binding survives and a retry with different child facts reattaches to the one child | `TestR2ProbeCrashBeforeCommit`, `TestR2ProbeCrashAfterCommit` |\n53|| My real SIGKILL at both Supersede seams | kill after stage → old binding (op1) intact; kill after rename → new binding (op2) complete; never torn | `TestR2ProbeSupersedeCrashSeams` |\n54|| Identical retries with different child facts ×3 | same inode, same mtime, same bytes, 1 directory entry | `TestR2ProbeIdenticalRetryInodeCensus` |\n55|| Receipt shape / PID | seven closed members; `pid`/`handle` appear only in comments | `logs/80-hygiene.log` |\n56|| Changed paths | exactly the 22 candidate paths; `internal/traceability` untouched; `task-board.config.json` equal to base; 0 `__pycache__`/`.pyc` in the tree | `logs/80` |\n57|| README package section | test + harness commands present; \"no `ax` command, no `doctor` result, no runtime capability claim\"; the sentinel/`managername` sentence is true as worded for the background path | `logs/80` |\n58|| Capability outside the closed §4.D set (`teleport`); descriptor generation ≠ host binding; invalid config + changed op; unverified + remote interactive | refused mismatch; refused `stale_generation`; `invalid_config` wins; `parked(restore_policy)` | `TestR2ProbeConflictingArmsAndClosedSets` |\n59|| Race gate `go test ./internal/sessquery -race -count=1 -timeout 25m` | **exit 0, `ok` in 494 s** on a loaded host (load 28→48, ~45 foreign `go test`/`.test` processes; not idle). The CR construction's own 27-command suite was green (`coverage_unit=exact_command_shard required=27 green=27`). Judgement: the rev1 red was a host-capacity artifact under the old 10m default, not a regression; with the 25m timeout the gate is green. | `logs/30-sessquery-race.log`, `logs/20-import-census.log` (axpane↔sessquery deps 0/0 both directions incl. test deps; candidate touches 0 sessquery bytes) |\n60|\n61|## P1 — must fix before this leaf can be accepted\n62|\n63|### P1-1 The bootstrap window, the checkpoint admission and the journal binding are keyed on the lease record's checkpoint, which is null for every epoch-1 owner forever (§13.1, §13.10, §13.11 step 5, §5.3, §5.7)\n64|`decide.go:507` (`bootstrapWindowClosed`), `decide.go:599` (`admitCheckpoint`)\n65|and `decide.go:571` (`checkMaterialization`) all read\n66|`Observation.Winner.HasCheckpoint`/`Winner.Checkpoint`. Lease records are\n67|immutable content-addressed blobs: `sessrepo.CreateLease` mints the epoch-1\n68|lease with a null checkpoint and only `CompareAndSwapLease` (the next epoch,\n69|a takeover) mints a lease that carries one (§5.3: \"Null only for epoch-1\n70|`create`; otherwise the validated materialized handoff base\"). Nothing ever\n71|writes a checkpoint onto the epoch-1 lease, however many checkpoints the\n72|session publishes. The landed fact for \"the newest checkpoint\" is the chain\n73|fold — `sessstate.Projection.HasCheckpoint`/`Newest` from\n74|`checkpoint.created`, checkpointed `session.stopped` and `session.resumed`\n75|(§5.7 `newest_checkpoint_id`, §14.4) — which this package already composes in\n76|`canAuthorParked` and never consults here. Consequences, all executed:\n77|\n78|- `TestN2ProbeEpochOneOwnerAfterCheckpoint` (`logs/11`): the ordinary\n79|  same-host story (created → idle → stopped with checkpoint C; landed engine\n80|  `state=stopped HasCheckpoint=true newest=C`; winning lease `epoch=1\n81|  HasCheckpoint=false`), then a restore with a new bootstrap operation and a\n82|  journal sourced from C → **`refused idempotency_mismatch` \"bootstrap\n83|  operation changed inside the bootstrap window\"**. The window never closes\n84|  on the creating host; the after-restore sequence is reachable only after a\n85|  takeover minted a successor lease. This is the rev1 P1-3 symptom for every\n86|  session that never changed hands.\n87|- Same probe, same state: a second attested checkpoint C2 of this session that\n88|  the chain never published (newest is C) → **`launch`**. \"Admit exactly the\n89|  winning lease's checkpoint\" admits anything when the lease carries none.\n90|- `TestN2ProbeNullLeaseCheckpointAdmitsCallerCheckpoint` (`logs/10`): restore,\n91|  epoch-1 winner, caller checkpoint the lease never published → `launch`;\n92|  committed journal sourced from `sha256:d2d2…` (a digest no lease and no\n93|  event names) → `launch`; through `Run` on the real stores → `launch` with a\n94|  bootstrap binding installed. §13.1: \"Captured objects may exist but no\n95|  Checkpoint Record is authoritative … objects are never relabeled as a\n96|  checkpoint\"; §13.11 step 5: \"validate the newest checkpoint\".\n97|- The committed positives pin this state as a launch:\n98|  `TestDecideTable/launch_restore_committed_checkpoint`,\n99|  `TestDecideAfterRestoreSequence/step3_resume_winning_lease_valid_materialization`\n100|  (journal `{Phase: committed}` with no source, epoch-1 winner) and\n101|  `TestRunRestoreCommitted` (epoch-1 lease, fixture journal sourced from\n102|  0xD2). The producer's window/admission tests close the window only through\n103|  `CompareAndSwapLease` successors. The matrix rows \"Checkpoint is the winning\n104|  lease's and names this session\", \"Materialization bound to the lease\n105|  checkpoint\", \"Idempotent … window closes on winner checkpoint\" and\n106|  \"After-restore sequence 1-5\" are therefore not faithfully driven.\n107|\n108|The rework brief's hint (\"using the winner's own `HasCheckpoint`/epoch already\n109|present in `Observation`\") is only sufficient for epoch ≥ 2; the fixtures'\n110|own epoch-1 lease could never have closed the window, which the producer did\n111|not notice. Required: derive the newest checkpoint through the landed chain\n112|fold (`sessstate.Reduce` → `Projection.HasCheckpoint`/`Newest.ID`; a\n113|successor lease's `Checkpoint` is the handoff base and must agree with it),\n114|close the window on that fact (epoch ≥ 2 implies it), admit exactly that checkpoint for a required\n115|checkpoint, bind a required journal's `SourceCheckpointID` to it, and park\n116|`restore_policy` when it is null and a checkpoint/materialization is required\n117|(the only launch-class path left in that state is the bootstrap retry without a\n118|checkpoint). Re-pin the three positives with the chain carrying the checkpoint,\n119|add the epoch-1-owner negatives (window, admission, journal — Decide and Run),\n120|and ship narrowing mutants on each of the three conditionals.\n121|\n122|## P2 — fix in the same rework\n123|\n124|### P2-1 Post-window supersession destroys the prior pair's receipt (§4.1, §4.C create/restore rows)\n125|`Supersede` (`binding.go:221`) renames the new receipt over the one\n126|`binding.json` per session; the superseded `(session_id,\n127|bootstrap_operation_id)` receipt is gone.\n128|\n129|- `TestN2ProbeSupersededPairIdenticalRetry` (`logs/10`): post-window, op2\n130|  launches (instance `…2222`), op3 launches (instance `…3333`), then an\n131|  **identical retry of op2 launches a third child** (instance `…4444`) instead\n132|  of replaying op2's receipt; `Status` afterwards identifies only the last\n133|  child. §4.1: \"An identical retry returns or reattaches to the one recorded\n134|  wrapper/child\"; §4.C: \"persist receipt before `wrapper_started`; identical\n135|  retry replays it\" — the key is `session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id`,\n136|  one receipt per pair.\n137|- `TestN2ProbePostWindowConcurrentDifferentOps`: two `Supersede` calls with\n138|  different operations both succeed (rename-over carries no no-replace\n139|  guard); nothing in the store or in `Run` orders two post-window wrappers.\n140|\n141|The rework brief allowed \"key the receipt per operation … or supersede it\",\n142|so this is P2, not P1; but supersession as implemented breaks the per-pair\n143|replay the same §4.C row requires. Keep the superseded receipts (per-operation\n144|files under the session directory, or an append-only receipt set) so an\n145|identical retry of any recorded pair reattaches to its own child, and make the\n146|post-window install no-replace per pair.\n147|\n148|### P2-2 `Run` silently derives the launch profile from the session head when no checkpoint store is bound (§13.10, §2.4)\n149|`run.go:190`: the winner's closure is loaded only `if … && stores.Ckpt != nil`;\n150|otherwise `deriveProfile` falls back to `sessprofile.Derive` over the head.\n151|\n152|- `TestN2ProbeNoCkptStoreProfileFallsBackToHead` (`logs/11`): winner carries\n153|  the checkpoint, authoritative head-only `profile.changed` under the winner,\n154|  `stores.Ckpt = nil` → `launch` with `yolo/E2` (the head pair). The same\n155|  request with the store bound carries `standard/null` (the closure). An\n156|  absent store is unknown, not \"no closure\": mirror the `CheckpointRequired`\n157|  guard at `run.go:169` and fail the run when the winner carries a checkpoint\n158|  and no checkpoint store is bound.\n159|\n160|## P3\n161|\n162|- **P3-1** The losing-epoch arm of the `Emit` mutation gate is unpinned.\n163|  `TestEmitUnderLosingLeaseRefuses` uses the `creating` chain, so it refuses\n164|  at the fold pre-check (\"does not fold from the derived lifecycle state\"),\n165|  never at `AuthorizeMutation`. My mutant RV7 (skip the gate when\n166|  `Presented.Epoch < Winner.Epoch`) SURVIVED the whole committed suite twice;\n167|  under it a losing-lease append is accepted under both a remote and a local\n168|  successor winner (`logs/53`). The gate itself is sound on the pristine tree\n169|  (`TestR2ProbeLosingLeaseReachesMutationGate`). Fix the test (foldable chain)\n170|  or add the RV7 row to the shipped harness.\n171|- **P3-2** Create-from-stopped through `Run` is unpinned: RV11 (Run's\n172|  supersede path narrowed to restore mode) SURVIVED twice; on the pristine\n173|  tree `TestN2ProbeCreateFromStoppedPostWindow` launches with a superseded\n174|  binding, under the mutant `Run` errors `idempotency_mismatch` from the store.\n175|  Add a launch-mode post-window `Run` test.\n176|- **P3-3** The coverage denominator was restated, not re-derived: the\n177|  TRACEABILITY acceptance table has **43 rows** (rev1's had 43 as well) while\n178|  results, TRACEABILITY and the matrix say \"41 of 41\". The rework brief\n179|  required re-deriving the ratio. My ratio: **39 of 43** driven faithfully —\n180|  rows \"Materialization validity gates local resume\", \"Checkpoint admission\n181|  gates resume\", \"After-restore sequence 1-5\" share P1-1; \"Bootstrap\n182|  idempotency\" carries P2-1.\n183|- **P3-4** Foreground credential-requiring path: `checkRealm` composes the\n184|  §4.C \"`credential_capable_execution_realm` when provider credentials are\n185|  required\" conditional only for background callers. A foreground caller with\n186|  `Smoke.Required`, a cached passing `resumesmoke` record and caller-supplied\n187|  `Target` claims (generation/OS are `Input` members, not attested evidence)\n188|  launches without the admitted row\n189|  (`TestN2ProbeForegroundCredentialPathWithoutRealmRow`). The README sentence\n190|  (\"no cached sentinel, `managername` observation, or bare boolean\") stays\n191|  true as worded; state this reading as a bound in TRACEABILITY or compose the\n192|  row when `Smoke.Required` regardless of caller.\n193|- **P3-5** `checkRealmBinding` returns on the first\n194|  `credential_capable_execution_realm` object: with two admitted realm objects\n195|  the outcome depends on input order (first foreign binding → refused; first\n196|  this-host → launch; `TestN2ProbeRealmEvidenceOrder`). Safe direction only;\n197|  iterate and accept when any admitted object binds this host+build.\n198|- **P3-6** An expired or pre-reboot realm row refuses as\n199|  `terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch` / `terminal_backend_stale_generation`\n200|  (Reconcile's first failure), not the §4.2 `capability_unavailable` with typed\n201|  realm/readiness details. Fail-closed, but the typed refusal the spec names is\n202|  not produced; document as a bound or filter dead evidence before reconcile.\n203|- **P3-7** Test hygiene: `TestRunTakeoverOfferEmitsParked` asserts a\n204|  non-interactive remote park with no emission (name is stale);\n205|  `TestRunPostWindowSupersedes` carries a stream-of-consciousness comment and\n206|  drops the materialization requirement instead of sourcing the journal from\n207|  the winner's checkpoint (my `TestR2ProbePostWindowRestoreWithSourcedJournal`\n208|  shows the full path launches).\n209|- **P3-8** LOGBOOK: the rev1 entry's F1 (\"both offers still author\n210|  `session.parked` with `remote_owner`\") is now false; the rev2 entry reverses\n211|  it only implicitly. Say so explicitly in the rev2 entry.\n212|\n213|## Coverage statement\n214|\n215|Producer claim: 41 of 41 AC rows driven. The table has 43 rows. Honest ratio:\n216|**39 of 43** (see P3-3). RM1/RM2/RM4 die; the composition holds under every\n217|bypass I planted except the null-checkpoint conditional (P1-1).\n218|\n219|## Instruments (all in the evidence archive)\n220|\n221|`probes/zz_review2_probe_test.go` (29 probes: 18 `TestR2Probe*` rev1 re-runs\n222|adapted to the new surface, 11 `TestN2Probe*` new plants; `TestN2ProbeStaleLocalPresentedAuthorsUnderWinner` is a harness fault — a chain the landed reducer refuses — superseded by `TestN2ProbeStaleLocalPresentedSameEpoch`), `review2_mutants.py` (12 rows, whole-suite\n223|killer), `delta_under_mutant.py`, `logs/10-11` (probe runs), `logs/40-42`\n224|(shipped harness ×2 + blob OIDs), `logs/50-53` (my mutants ×2 + delta\n225|witnesses), `logs/60` (crash reruns), `logs/70-71` (tree-exact checks, six\n226|packages), `logs/80-81` (hygiene, TRACEABILITY name/row census), `logs/20`,\n227|`logs/30` (import census, race gate), `REVIEW-MANIFEST.txt`.\n228|\n229|Verdict recorded by RUN-260917-368f1f; no product edits, commits, checkpoints\n230|or integration were performed; the isolated copies are deleted after\n231|attachment.","final_result":true}}}
