{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c779","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b131-d4f6-7b82-a7a6-5363cf3ac7fb"},"sequence":535,"recorded_at":1780531400001065,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"2237b1e3-856b-4a22-9f46-61adba667efd","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"2237b1e3-856b-4a22-9f46-61adba667efd","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"2237b1e3-856b-4a22-9f46-61adba667efd"},"call_id":"call_01a0b13401fa75549697c61d6d6d8925","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-20-1\",\n  \"command\": \"sed -n '100,212p' /tmp/my-readme.diff; echo =====LOGBOOK=====; cat /tmp/my-logbook.diff\",\n  \"description\": \"Show remaining README and LOGBOOK diffs\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"+per-row verdicts with subprocess exits; `AX_MUTANT_VERBOSE=1` additionally\\n+prints the raw per-plant logs. Task validation logs and mutation artifacts are\\n+attached to `TASK-260830-1geqhj`. The package adds no `ax` command, no\\n+`doctor` result, and no runtime capability claim; the clause-to-test matrix\\n+with its stated bounds lives in\\n+[the task evidence map](internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md).\\n+\\n ## Ownership reducer properties\\n \\n The four story-pinned ownership invariants (pinned v0.6.0 Sections 2.2, 5.3,\\n@@ -3011,9 +3056,9 @@ go test ./internal/cliresult -cover -count=1\\n ## Generated Contract Catalogs\\n \\n [`internal/catalog`](internal/catalog) exposes typed records through\\n-`catalog.Current()` for v0.7.0 and `catalog.ForRelease()` for the exact pinned\\n-v0.6.0, v0.5.0 and v0.4.3 compatibility projections. The reviewed input is\\n-[`catalog.v0.7.0.json`](internal/catalog/catalog.v0.7.0.json); generation first\\n+`catalog.Current()` for v0.5.0 and `catalog.ForRelease()` for the exact pinned\\n+v0.4.3 compatibility projection. The reviewed input is\\n+[`catalog.v0.5.0.json`](internal/catalog/catalog.v0.5.0.json); generation first\\n verifies the exact [`specpin`](internal/specpin) lock, strictly rejects partial,\\n unknown, substituted, duplicate, release-incompatible, or unreviewed semantic\\n metadata through a canonical projection digest, then writes\\n@@ -3023,8 +3068,6 @@ semantic identity.\\n \\n | Release projection | Contracts | Operations | Capability names | Events | Error codes |\\n | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\\n-| v0.7.0 | 64 | 99 | 46 | 112 | 109 |\\n-| v0.6.0 | 63 | 99 | 46 | 112 | 109 |\\n | v0.5.0 | 60 | 99 | 46 | 112 | 109 |\\n | v0.4.3 | 55 | 89 | 30 | 112 | 94 |\\n \\n@@ -3051,21 +3094,21 @@ adopted release, so the check stays valid when the adopted release changes.\\n The explicit equivalent pins the same inputs by path:\\n \\n ```bash\\n-go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -metadata internal/catalog/catalog.v0.7.0.json -contracts internal/specpin/v0.7.0.lock.json -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\\n+go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -metadata internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json -contracts internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\\n ```\\n \\n ## Specification-to-Code Ownership Gate\\n \\n [`internal/traceability`](internal/traceability) provides the read-only\\n repository gate used by CI. Its reviewed\\n-[`ownership.v0.7.0.json`](internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json)\\n-registry independently enumerates implementation owners for all 64 current\\n-contract rows, 36 pinned or catalog-referenced normative section keys, 135\\n-executable acceptance cases, 68 exact section bindings with their declared\\n-coverage, 7 disclosed unowned sections, and 33 exact fixture identities or\\n+[`ownership.v0.6.0.json`](internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json)\\n+registry independently enumerates implementation owners for all 63 current\\n+contract rows, 36 pinned or catalog-referenced normative section keys, 132\\n+executable acceptance cases, 65 exact section bindings with their declared\\n+coverage, 7 disclosed unowned sections, and 32 exact fixture identities or\\n Appendix D anchors. The v0.4.3 projection is checked as an owned 55-contract subset,\\n-and the superseded v0.6.0 and v0.5.0 registries are checked as owned legacy projections.\\n-The generated v0.7.0 catalog also carries the reviewed schema/version/self-field\\n+and the superseded v0.5.0 registry is checked as an owned legacy projection.\\n+The generated v0.6.0 catalog also carries the reviewed schema/version/self-field\\n contracts used by canonical object identity calculation; generator validation\\n binds each row to a pinned contract and rejects duplicate, unsupported,\\n malformed, or digest-drifted metadata.\\n@@ -3084,7 +3127,7 @@ go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck -section 6.2\\n \\n The repeated `-section` form is the Story-scope production gate. It resolves\\n each assigned subsection, and every heading in a same-top-level range, against\\n-the immutable v0.7.0 inventory. Every exact `section_binding` must name its own\\n+the immutable v0.5.0 inventory. Every exact `section_binding` must name its own\\n production declaration and executable acceptance case, and must additionally\\n discharge the whole section it claims. A generic top-level source pin is not a\\n scoped implementation owner. Malformed, nonexistent, unpinned, or otherwise\\n@@ -3162,10 +3205,10 @@ useful is admitted, and the gate cannot decide otherwise.\\n `tracecheck` prints the ratio it measured rather than a sentence about it:\\n \\n ```text\\n-section coverage: bindings=68 full=2 partial=6 sliver=4 unevidenced=52 unmeasured=4 unowned=7 clauses_discharged=49/569\\n+section coverage: bindings=65 full=2 partial=6 sliver=4 unevidenced=49 unmeasured=4 unowned=7 clauses_discharged=49/535\\n ```\\n \\n-Sixty-eight section bindings discharge 49 of the 569 normative clauses their\\n+Sixty-five section bindings discharge 49 of the 535 normative clauses their\\n sections carry. Two bindings are `full` (Section 6.2, whose single clause is the\\n native-Windows `conpty` requirement, discharged by the positive\\n `TestEveryPinnedReaderHasPositiveNativeWindowsAndWSL2Lanes` lanes together\\n@@ -3227,26 +3270,19 @@ single-owner, replica-restraint, winning-epoch-carriage, and\\n losing-event-rejection invariants while the replication, secret, store,\\n and directory invariants have no implementation), four are `unmeasured` (Sections 7.3, 13.12, 13.14.5 and 15.2, each of\\n which carries a gap saying why the scanner measures zero and what is missing),\\n-and fifty-two are `unevidenced`. Seven sections are recorded unowned.\\n+and forty-nine are `unevidenced`. Seven sections are recorded unowned.\\n All 13 sections added by v0.6.0 name pending task owners in the reviewed\\n registry gaps; these assignments grant no runtime admission. The\\n [adoption ownership map](internal/traceability/adoption-v0.6.0.md) separates\\n shared runtime APIs, their callers, product conformance and upstream source\\n publication validators, and preserves historical acceptance obligations.\\n-The v0.7.0 revision adds no numbered section; its launch-plan, stdin,\\n-caller_launch_plan, environment_drift and curator-run clause areas name\\n-pending story owners in the reviewed registry gaps, and these assignments\\n-grant no runtime admission either. The\\n-[adoption ownership map](internal/traceability/adoption-v0.7.0.md) attributes\\n-each clause area to its implementing story and records the shared-section\\n-splits.\\n Assigned-scope admission therefore succeeds today for `-section 6.2` and\\n `-section 2.4` and nothing else; every other assignment is refused with its\\n ratio and its gap.\\n A `partial` binding is refused by assigned-scope admission exactly like an\\n `unevidenced` one: admission requires `full`.\\n \\n-Two admitted bindings out of sixty-eight cover five clauses, and that is\\n+Two admitted bindings out of sixty-five cover five clauses, and that is\\n disclosed here rather than hidden: without Section 6.2 the admit path would only\\n ever be exercised synthetically. Its discharge is no longer positive-only: the\\n native-Windows lanes carry the positive arm and\\n=====LOGBOOK=====\\ndiff --git a/LOGBOOK.md b/LOGBOOK.md\\nindex 8022478..d57be37 100644\\n--- a/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n@@ -5,21 +5,22 @@\\n \\n ## 2026-09-17\\n \\n-### TASK-260917-10k118: reconstructed the reviewed v0.7.0 adoption on trunk 7efe385 (STORY-260916-3uqbwq unlandable, accepted CRs frozen)\\n-- METHOD: true pin delta is `git diff e4e3e88 9cb5dd4` (10 files) — the exported 238-file patch diffs unrelated tips and would revert five landed stories, so it was used as transport only; rev3 candidate bytes applied (15 modified + 3 new) with the 5 trunk-merged files copied verbatim after diff-review (no trunk test lost, `task-board.config.json` untouched). All 19 machine-applied files `cmp`-identical to the rev3 bytes; ownership sha256 `2548870d…8a5070`, projection digest `c4cd46bf…53473f6` recomputed two independent ways.\\n-- RE-VERIFIED (this session, fresh clone + production helpers): tag `d4abe46f…795b3` Good, peeled `32b3f2ba…321834`, SPEC blob `c4903e60…1ddd86` 1185291 bytes sha256 `c6b2fe64…89ddcf` byte-identical to `SPEC.v0.7.0.md`; lock 64/64 rows order- and set-identical to the §1.5 table (1 known order normalization); 65/65 bindings + 132/132 cases carried with 3 reviewed additions each; all 49 discharged clauses re-measured (uniform +20/+79/+185/+281/+392, excerpts verbatim); rev3 prose says \\\"48 carried clause lines\\\" in two places — measured 49, matching the 49/569 numerator; artifact is right, prose miscounted.\\n-- FINDING F1: the reviewed v0.7.0 source normative-section group keeps production `VerifyV060` while its cases moved to the v0.7.0 pair; the v0.5.0→v0.6.0 precedent moved `Verify`→`VerifyV060`, so the pattern says `VerifyV070`. Green because the gate checks declaration existence only. Reviewed bytes are not rewritten in a reconstruction; the new re-derivation test pins the carried reference literally with the rationale.\\n-- NEW TESTS (this Story's scope): `TestV070RegistryRederivesFromTrunkV060Registry` (carry completeness, clause re-measurement via production inventory+quote, no self-minted claims) and `TestREADMEMeasuredCoverageMatchesTracecheckReport` (fenced line byte-equal to tool output, 8 headline prose figures re-derived). Narrowing mutants per test + token-preserving README plant with full behavioral suites; harmless controls SURVIVED. Full 27-command suite green on the exact tree.\\n-- FIGURES: contracts=64, acceptance cases=135, bindings=68, clauses 49/569. No launch-plan/stdin/caller_launch_plan/environment_drift/curator-run runtime claim.\\n-- STATUS: implemented, tests green, ready for review; work left UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for the handoff snapshot.\\n-\\n-### TASK-260916-n9r71p: bound v0.7.0 launch-plan catalog row and curator story owners\\n-- AUTHORITY: catalogue generation, Current, CI roots and traceability consume the adopted v0.7.0 lock/document/inventory; four release projections preserve V060/V050/V043 history. Metadata digest `c4094101…50274a35`; ownership digest `c4cd46bf…53473f6`. Localstore stays on explicit CurrentV050. Validation command 22 is the release-agnostic `-adopted` gate, which resolves to the v0.7.0 metadata/lock pair on this tree.\\n-- DELTA: +Launch Plan request `urn:ax:schema:launch-plan-request` 1.0.0 (64th row, census-only, no catalog family); provider families carry the 2.1.0/3.1.0 minors (SPEC 7.5 adds members not operations; consumers range over names); session-record 3.1.0, error 1.4.0/1.5.0 and manifest/probe 1.1.0 stay census-only (carrying 3.1.0 panics canonicaljson init — no Go shape validator yet — same init-panic rationale as error 1.4.0). +3 section bindings (13.1, 13.10, 14.1), +1 fixture (`pin:ax-launch-plan-request-v1`), gaps updated for 5.1/7.3/7.4/7.5/appendix-d with story owners; 48 carried clause lines re-measured against SPEC.v0.7.0.md (uniform +20/+79/+185/+281/+392 shifts, every excerpt verbatim, no ID shifts).\\n-- OWNERS: all 7 launch-plan clause areas name implementing EPIC-260916-18uelk stories with unevidenced coverage — 3fjjtn parsing/refusals (14.1, 13.1, contract), 2q85nu record embedding (5.1), 1kp1lx stdin/replay (7.5), 1ea7od plugin capability (7.3/7.4), 3aukw3 drift (13.10), 3ustb3 naming (13.1 split), vucwn0 vectors (fixture, appendix-d split). The source-derived AdoptedSections test requires 6/6 plus 2 split attributions and refuses each through VerifyAssignedSections.\\n-- HISTORY: registry re-derived from the trunk-final v0.6.0 registry, carrying the five landed stories' 31 acceptance cases and 9 section bindings (2.2, 2.4, 5.3/5.4/5.5, 6.6, 7.7, 8, 10.6, 11.10.1–4, 13.12/13.13, 16.1) with re-measured clause lines; v0.6.0/v0.5.0 locks, registries, readers and historical tests byte-untouched versus trunk; the v0.7.0 inventory is identifier-equal to v0.6.0 (170 ids, same digest), so legacy verification derives both historical registries from the adopted lock. P3 closed: pin.go/specdoc.go consumer comments now true in the present tense; section:11.10.5 carried as a Disclosure owner (source evidence only, no implementation claim).\\n-- FIGURES: contracts=64, normative section keys=36, acceptance cases=135, fixtures=33, historical contracts=55; bindings=68 (full=2, partial=6, sliver=4, unevidenced=52, unmeasured=4), unowned=7, discharged clauses=49/569. No launch-plan/stdin/caller_launch_plan/environment_drift/curator-run runtime claim anywhere.\\n-- STATUS: implemented, tests green, ready for review; work left UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for the handoff snapshot.\\n+### TASK-260830-1geqhj rev2 — ax pane rework: authority, window, closure, realm\\n+- REWORKED on `888ae3d` after review-verdict-rev1 (18 findings): event authority through `fencing.AuthorizeMutation` with local-hold-only emission and the §5.7 fold gate (`sessstate.Reduce`); realm authorization through the admitted `credential_capable_execution_realm` row bound to host binding/build/generation (bare boolean removed); bootstrap window closed by the winner's `HasCheckpoint` with atomic `Supersede`; checkpoint admission bound to the winning lease and session; profile from the checkpoint closure (`DeriveForHeads`); journal source bound to the lease checkpoint; non-interactive `headless_creation` conditional; remote non-interactive parks per §4.2 step 5.\\n+- F1: a park decision's stale/unverified presented token never authors — `Emit` presents the winning tuple itself, so verified local-winner parks (stale, material, checkpoint) emit while remote/unverified/ambiguous/handoff parks refuse; `Run` pre-checks local hold + foldability and parks without evidence rather than manufacturing a §5.2 collision.\\n+- F2: the bootstrap window is the winner's `HasCheckpoint`, not a clock: in-window changed ops refuse `idempotency_mismatch` in both modes, post-window new ops supersede via staged rename; the `binding-*.tmp` sweep is age-gated (1 min) so a concurrent live stage is never deleted.\\n+- F3: resume profile is the checkpoint closure, not the head: `Run` loads the winner's heads even when the checkpoint is not otherwise required, so a head-only or losing-lease `profile.changed` never drives launch (§2.4, §13.10).\\n+- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 35 narrowing mutants, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 36/36 with control); reviewer's RM1/RM2/RM4 survivors now killed by `TestRunTornLeasePropagates`, `TestDecideRemoteOwnerPrecedesMaterialization`, `TestDecideRestoreChangedOperationRefuses`. AC 41/41 re-derived with the six previously unfaithful rows re-pinned.\\n+- Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n+\\n+### TASK-260830-1geqhj — ax pane enforcement wrapper validation core (first leaf)\\n+- DELIVERED: `internal/axpane` — the pure `Decide` core (`launch|reattach|attach_remote|takeover_offer|parked|refused`), the `Run` orchestration over real stores, the durable bootstrap `(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)` binding store, §5.2 event authorship, and the §7.A descriptor builder. Every check composes a landed gate (`fencing`, `matjournal`, `sessckpt`/`sessrepo`, `sessprofile`, `provhost`, `resumesmoke`, `terminalbackend`, `config`, `axerror`); nothing is re-implemented. First leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe; `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract (final leaf re-pins).\\n+- F1: `fencing` launch entries refuse — not park — foreign sessions, malformed tokens, and lapsed grants, so the wrapper's `refused(lease_conflict)` rows for foreign/expired inputs compose directly; only remote/ambiguous/unverified/absent/stale ownership parks. Remote parks resolve locally to `attach_remote` (interactive + attach admitted) or `takeover_offer`, and both offers still author `session.parked` with `remote_owner`.\\n+- F2: the tuple gate must precede profile mapping in arm order: `ResolveMapping` re-checks the tuple internally, so mapping-first would wear tuple refusals as `profile_mapping_unavailable`. The standalone `CheckResumeTuple` call stays as fail-fast ordering; weakening it alone is unobservable (defense in depth, stated in TRACEABILITY.md).\\n+- F3: `terminalbackend.Reconcile` maps generation drift to the more specific `terminal_backend_stale_generation` (not the generic mismatch), and `create` is conferred by both `durable_disconnect` and `headless_creation` — the unproven vector must deny both. `sessckpt.Get` re-attests through `sessrepo` on every read, so checkpoint admission composes through the read path.\\n+- F4: `Bind` is linearizable on the commit race via link-EEXIST re-read (same operation reattaches to the winner, changed operation refuses); the `AfterStage` hook plays the concurrent winner deterministically in tests. The store stamps `created_at` itself — scalar timestamps require ≥3 fractional digits, so `time.RFC3339Nano` (which omits trailing zeros) is not a valid stamp.\\n+- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 24 narrowing mutants, all KILLED by named tests through `internal/axpane/mutant_harness.py`, plus the applied harmless SURVIVED control (25/25 rows match; per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits in the outcome tar). No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text.\\n+- AC: 41 of 41 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md`); crash/idempotency evidence via the no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-kill pattern. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n \\n ### TASK-260830-2x16gz — hostile-network conformance suite + AC-HOST-001 (final leaf)\\n - DELIVERED: `internal/hostchannel/hostile_test.go` + `hostile_carrier_test.go` re-derive all seven story cases through the real `Dial`/`Serve`/`Call` entries with per-vector Section 15 classes and state censuses, and execute the AC-HOST-001 rows: real OpenSSH loopback carrier (unprivileged `sshd`, forced command, exact `ServeArgv` on the wire, TLS-first bytes, no PTY, bounded stderr), rotation/enrollment lifecycle, copied-key halves, revocation fencing, stale-read integrity, recovery bypasses, concurrency/stall races, role swap, and the v4 loader gate. Test-only leaf; no production file changed. P3 notes closed (`ax-host/2` vector, bad-destination deadline hook).\\n@@ -447,15 +448,6 @@\\n - AC: 19 of 21 enumerated production acceptance rows are driven by named production-entry tests and pass. Rows 15 (Windows runtime ACL equivalence) and 21 (consumer/diagnostic export surfaces outside this repository) remain explicit bounds. This is the accepted scope boundary; RPC/TLS/hello/dispatch/stream lifecycle remains with its owning task.\\n - HANDOFF: outcome evidence is ready for independent review. This entry does not claim review acceptance, main integration, or delivery.\\n \\n-### TASK-260916-2yzf5d: adopted signed v0.7.0 normative source alongside v0.5.0/v0.6.0, no consumer re-pointed\\n-- PROVENANCE (verified this session, upstream read-only): `git tag -v v0.7.0` Good (tag object `d4abe46f…795b3`, ECDSA `SHA256:V6JiKG7J29mjsvikcLoSVp0bLa77VTsFy12gnLO81cM`, tagger Ivan Oparin), peeled commit `32b3f2ba…321834`, SPEC.md blob `c4903e60…1ddd86` 1185291 bytes SHA256 `c6b2fe64…89ddcf` measured from the tagged blob (zero CR bytes, raw == LF-normalized).\\n-- SCOPE: `internal/specpin/{pin,sections}.go` + `v0.7.0.lock.json` (64 contracts, 6 fixtures), `internal/specdoc/{specdoc.go,SPEC.v0.7.0.md}` + `pin070_test.go`, `sections070_test.go`, `specdoc070_test.go`, README provenance paragraphs, this entry. `v0.5.0`/`v0.6.0` locks, documents, readers and all existing tests byte-untouched in behavior.\\n-- DELTA (measured, SPEC §1.5 cross-checked row-for-row in order, lock registry verified against the spec table by script): +Launch Plan request `urn:ax:schema:launch-plan-request` 1.0.0 (between Session record and Session event); Session record +3.1.0, Provider protocol +2.1.0/+3.1.0, Provider manifest/probe +1.1.0, Structured error +1.5.0, CLI result unchanged at 5.0.0; +0 numbered sections (only an unnumbered `#### Caller launch-plan code` and appendix subsection A.12, both excluded by the inventory rule — the 170-identifier inventory digest is measured equal to v0.6.0's and pinned independently); +1 fixture (`ax-launch-plan-request-v1` `ec4310b8…`), host-channel/selector fixture digests move for a `specification_version` 0.7.0 bump only, 3 old fixture files byte-identical upstream. v0.4.3 compatibility grows to 9 absent + 9 overrides exactly as the v0.7.0 historical account states.\\n-- HISTORY: v0.7.0 projections of v0.6.0 (63 rows), v0.5.0 (60 rows) and v0.4.3 (55 rows) are `reflect.DeepEqual` to the real locks/projections — adoption cannot rewrite history. `ContractsForRelease(v0.7.0)` on a v0.5.0 or v0.6.0 manifest is refused: a stale pin cannot authorize the new release. Launch-plan/stdin/caller_launch_plan/environment_drift runtime supp