lease checkpoint; non-interactive `headless_creation` conditional; remote non-interactive parks per §4.2 step 5.\\n- F1: a park decision's stale/unverified presented token never authors — `Emit` presents the winning tuple itself, so verified local-winner parks (stale, material, checkpoint) emit while remote/unverified/ambiguous/handoff parks refuse; `Run` pre-checks local hold + foldability and parks without evidence rather than manufacturing a §5.2 collision.\\n- F2: the bootstrap window is the winner's `HasCheckpoint`, not a clock: in-window changed ops refuse `idempotency_mismatch` in both modes, post-window new ops supersede via staged rename; the `binding-*.tmp` sweep is age-gated (1 min) so a concurrent live stage is never deleted.\\n- F3: resume profile is the checkpoint closure, not the head: `Run` loads the winner's heads even when the checkpoint is not otherwise required, so a head-only or losing-lease `profile.changed` never drives launch (§2.4, §13.10).\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 1936,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 484,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
