{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c9b3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b131-d4f6-7b82-a7a6-5363cf3ac7fb"},"sequence":820,"recorded_at":1780531400001635,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"2237b1e3-856b-4a22-9f46-61adba667efd","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"2237b1e3-856b-4a22-9f46-61adba667efd","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"2237b1e3-856b-4a22-9f46-61adba667efd"},"call_id":"call_01a0b135166c76b8aaf6d95328412afe","text":"Read text file `internal/axpane/run.go`.\n1|package axpane\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"errors\"\n5|\t\"fmt\"\n6|\n7|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/config\"\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/fencing\"\n9|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessrepo\"\n10|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminalbackend\"\n11|)\n12|\n13|// Request is the complete Run surface: the session and bootstrap\n14|// operation under decision plus every modeled-caller fact the\n15|// adapters cannot load from the durable stores (sync state,\n16|// provider build and identity, backend documents, realm readiness,\n17|// presentation geometry). The stores supply configuration,\n18|// sessions, leases, journals, checkpoints, and bindings.\n19|type Request struct {\n20|\tSessionID            string\n21|\tBootstrapOperationID string\n22|\tMode                 Mode\n23|\n24|\tConfigInputs    config.Inputs\n25|\tConfigOverrides config.Overrides\n26|\n27|\t// Presented is the local fencing token; Observe carries the\n28|\t// caller-reported sync, handoff, grant, and clock facts.\n29|\tPresented fencing.PresentedToken\n30|\tObserve   fencing.ObserveInput\n31|\n32|\t// Materialization selects the required journal: when Required\n33|\t// is set the adapter loads ID and the decision requires the\n34|\t// committed phase (after-restore step 3).\n35|\tMaterializationID       string\n36|\tMaterializationRequired bool\n37|\n38|\t// Checkpoint selects the resume checkpoint: when Required is\n39|\t// set the adapter loads ID and the decision admits it.\n40|\tCheckpointID       string\n41|\tCheckpointRequired bool\n42|\n43|\tProvider ProviderFacts\n44|\tSmoke    SmokeFacts\n45|\tRealm    Realm\n46|\tBackend  BackendFacts\n47|\n48|\t// Entrypoint is the wrapper argv.\n49|\tEntrypoint []string\n50|\n51|\t// HostBinding is the AX-validated host-local binding subset\n52|\t// the supplied descriptor must match. Geometry and\n53|\t// interactivity shape the supplied descriptor; InstanceID\n54|\t// pins the terminal instance, or mints a fresh UUIDv7 when\n55|\t// empty.\n56|\tHostBinding terminalbackend.InstanceBinding\n57|\tInteractive bool\n58|\tColumns     uint16\n59|\tRows        uint16\n60|\tInstanceID  string\n61|\n62|\t// RemoteInteractive reports that the remote owner holds the\n63|\t// session in an interactive terminal (after-restore step 4).\n64|\tRemoteInteractive bool\n65|\n66|\t// LocalHostID authors parked events; CreatedAt stamps them.\n67|\tLocalHostID string\n68|\tCreatedAt   string\n69|\n70|\t// Hooks arms the bootstrap binding crash boundaries.\n71|\tHooks *Hooks\n72|}\n73|\n74|// Outcome is the one Run result: the decision plus the durable\n75|// effects it authorized. Exactly one effect applies: a launch binds\n76|// the bootstrap pair (superseding after the window closed), a\n77|// reattach returns the recorded binding, a parked or remote-offer\n78|// decision with a locally held, verified winner and a foldable\n79|// lifecycle authors the parked event, and every other outcome\n80|// writes nothing.\n81|type Outcome struct {\n82|\tDecision Decision\n83|\t// Binding is the bound receipt on launch and the recorded\n84|\t// receipt on reattach, nil otherwise.\n85|\tBinding *Binding\n86|\t// Event is the authored parked event reference and bytes;\n87|\t// Emitted is false when the decision parks without a locally\n88|\t// held winner, without a foldable lifecycle, or when the\n89|\t// outcome is neither parked nor a remote offer. A park without\n90|\t// chain authority parks without evidence, never by manufacturing\n91|\t// a sequence collision under another host's lease.\n92|\tEvent     *sessrepo.EventRef\n93|\tEventJSON []byte\n94|\tEmitted   bool\n95|}\n96|\n97|// Run orchestrates the wrapper: validate configuration, load the\n98|// logical session, prove the bootstrap binding state, observe the\n99|// winning lease, load materialization, checkpoint, and profile\n100|// state, decide through the pure core, then apply exactly the\n101|// authorized durable effect. A store failure propagates as an\n102|// error with no decision: unknown is never absence and never a\n103|// launch.\n104|func Run(stores Stores, request Request) (Outcome, error) {\n105|\tempty := Outcome{}\n106|\tif stores.Repo == nil || stores.Pane == nil {\n107|\t\treturn empty, fmt.Errorf(\"axpane run carries no repository or binding store\")\n108|\t}\n109|\t// The request hooks arm a copy of the binding handle: Run never\n110|\t// mutates the caller's store.\n111|\tpane := *stores.Pane\n112|\tpaneStore := pane.WithHooks(request.Hooks)\n113|\tinput := Input{\n114|\t\tSessionID:               request.SessionID,\n115|\t\tBootstrapOperationID:    request.BootstrapOperationID,\n116|\t\tMode:                    request.Mode,\n117|\t\tPresented:               request.Presented,\n118|\t\tProvider:                request.Provider,\n119|\t\tSmoke:                   request.Smoke,\n120|\t\tRealm:                   request.Realm,\n121|\t\tBackend:                 request.Backend,\n122|\t\tEntrypoint:              request.Entrypoint,\n123|\t\tHostBinding:             request.HostBinding,\n124|\t\tRemoteInteractive:       request.RemoteInteractive,\n125|\t\tInteractive:             request.Interactive,\n126|\t\tCheckpointRequired:      request.CheckpointRequired,\n127|\t\tCheckpointID:            request.CheckpointID,\n128|\t\tMaterializationRequired: request.MaterializationRequired,\n129|\t}\n130|\tinput.ConfigErr = ValidateConfig(request.ConfigInputs, request.ConfigOverrides)\n131|\n132|\tknown, _, err := LoadSession(stores.Repo, request.SessionID)\n133|\tif err != nil {\n134|\t\treturn empty, err\n135|\t}\n136|\tinput.SessionKnown = known\n137|\n138|\texisting, found, err := paneStore.Status(request.SessionID)\n139|\tif err != nil {\n140|\t\treturn empty, err\n141|\t}\n142|\tif found {\n143|\t\tduplicate := existing\n144|\t\tinput.ExistingBinding = &duplicate\n145|\t}\n146|\n147|\tvar observation fencing.Observation\n148|\tif known {\n149|\t\tobserved, err := ObserveOwnership(stores.Repo, request.SessionID, request.Observe)\n150|\t\tif err != nil {\n151|\t\t\treturn empty, err\n152|\t\t}\n153|\t\tobservation = observed\n154|\t}\n155|\tinput.Observation = observation\n156|\n157|\tif request.MaterializationRequired {\n158|\t\tif stores.Mat == nil {\n159|\t\t\treturn empty, fmt.Errorf(\"axpane run requires a materialization with no journal store\")\n160|\t\t}\n161|\t\tjournal, admitted, err := LoadMaterialization(stores.Mat, request.MaterializationID)\n162|\t\tif err != nil {\n163|\t\t\treturn empty, err\n164|\t\t}\n165|\t\tinput.Journal = journal\n166|\t\tinput.JournalOK = admitted\n167|\t}\n168|\tif request.CheckpointRequired {\n169|\t\tif stores.Ckpt == nil {\n170|\t\t\treturn empty, fmt.Errorf(\"axpane run requires a checkpoint with no checkpoint store\")\n171|\t\t}\n172|\t\tdoc, err := LoadCheckpoint(stores.Ckpt, request.CheckpointID)\n173|\t\tif err != nil {\n174|\t\t\treturn empty, err\n175|\t\t}\n176|\t\tinput.CheckpointDoc = doc\n177|\t}\n178|\tif known {\n179|\t\trecord, events, err := LoadProfile(stores.Repo, request.SessionID)\n180|\t\tif err != nil {\n181|\t\t\treturn empty, err\n182|\t\t}\n183|\t\tinput.ProfileRecord = record\n184|\t\tinput.ProfileEvents = events\n185|\t\t// Resume derives the effective profile from the validated\n186|\t\t// checkpoint's event-head closure, never the session head,\n187|\t\t// so a head-only or losing-lease change cannot become the\n188|\t\t// launch profile (§13.10, §2.4). The heads come from the\n189|\t\t// winner's own checkpoint when the winner carries one.\n190|\t\tif observation.HasWinner && observation.Winner.HasCheckpoint && stores.Ckpt != nil {\n191|\t\t\tdoc := input.CheckpointDoc\n192|\t\t\tif !request.CheckpointRequired || request.CheckpointID != observation.Winner.Checkpoint {\n193|\t\t\t\tloaded, err := LoadCheckpoint(stores.Ckpt, observation.Winner.Checkpoint)\n194|\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n195|\t\t\t\t\treturn empty, err\n196|\t\t\t\t}\n197|\t\t\t\tdoc = loaded\n198|\t\t\t}\n199|\t\t\tif len(doc) > 0 {\n200|\t\t\t\theads, err := checkpointHeads(doc)\n201|\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n202|\t\t\t\t\treturn empty, err\n203|\t\t\t\t}\n204|\t\t\t\tinput.ProfileHeads = heads\n205|\t\t\t}\n206|\t\t} else if request.CheckpointRequired && len(input.CheckpointDoc) > 0 {\n207|\t\t\theads, err := checkpointHeads(input.CheckpointDoc)\n208|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n209|\t\t\t\treturn empty, err\n210|\t\t\t}\n211|\t\t\tinput.ProfileHeads = heads\n212|\t\t}\n213|\t}\n214|\n215|\tinstance := request.InstanceID\n216|\tif instance == \"\" {\n217|\t\tminted, err := MintInstanceIDRandom()\n218|\t\tif err != nil {\n219|\t\t\treturn empty, err\n220|\t\t}\n221|\t\tinstance = minted\n222|\t}\n223|\tdescriptorDoc, err := BuildDescriptor(DescriptorParams{\n224|\t\tBinding: BindingRef{\n225|\t\t\tBindingDigest:         request.HostBinding.TerminalBindingID,\n226|\t\t\tBackendID:             request.HostBinding.BackendID,\n227|\t\t\tImplementationVersion: request.HostBinding.ImplementationVersion,\n228|\t\t\tProtocolVersion:       request.HostBinding.ProtocolVersion,\n229|\t\t\tGeneration:            request.HostBinding.Generation,\n230|\t\t},\n231|\t\tInstanceID:  instance,\n232|\t\tInteractive: request.Interactive,\n233|\t\tColumns:     request.Columns,\n234|\t\tRows:        request.Rows,\n235|\t})\n236|\tif err != nil {\n237|\t\treturn empty, err\n238|\t}\n239|\tinput.Descriptor = descriptorDoc\n240|\n241|\tdecision := Decide(input)\n242|\toutcome := Outcome{Decision: decision}\n243|\tswitch decision.Action {\n244|\tcase ActionLaunch:\n245|\t\tcandidate := Binding{\n246|\t\t\tSessionID:          request.SessionID,\n247|\t\t\tOperationID:        request.BootstrapOperationID,\n248|\t\t\tTerminalInstanceID: instance,\n249|\t\t}\n250|\t\tcandidate.BindingDigest = BindingDigest(candidate)\n251|\t\t// A post-window launch with a recorded prior operation\n252|\t\t// supersedes the binding; every other launch binds\n253|\t\t// no-replace. The decision already applied the window\n254|\t\t// predicate, so a mismatch here is a concurrent commit\n255|\t\t// the retry observes through Status.\n256|\t\tif input.ExistingBinding != nil && input.ExistingBinding.OperationID != request.BootstrapOperationID {\n257|\t\t\tbound, err := paneStore.Supersede(request.SessionID, request.BootstrapOperationID, candidate)\n258|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n259|\t\t\t\treturn empty, err\n260|\t\t\t}\n261|\t\t\tduplicate := bound\n262|\t\t\toutcome.Binding = &duplicate\n263|\t\t\tbreak\n264|\t\t}\n265|\t\tbound, reattached, err := paneStore.Bind(request.SessionID, request.BootstrapOperationID, candidate)\n266|\t\tif err != nil {\n267|\t\t\t// A concurrent changed-operation commit surfaces\n268|\t\t\t// here as idempotency_mismatch: the caller's retry\n269|\t\t\t// observes the winner through Status and decides\n270|\t\t\t// the refused outcome.\n271|\t\t\treturn empty, err\n272|\t\t}\n273|\t\tif reattached {\n274|\t\t\t// A concurrent wrapper won the bind between Status\n275|\t\t\t// and Bind: the pair is bound, so this run\n276|\t\t\t// reattaches to the recorded child instead of\n277|\t\t\t// launching a second one.\n278|\t\t\toutcome.Decision.Action = ActionReattach\n279|\t\t\toutcome.Decision.Detail = \"reattach to the one recorded wrapper/child\"\n280|\t\t}\n281|\t\tduplicate := bound\n282|\t\toutcome.Binding = &duplicate\n283|\tcase ActionReattach:\n284|\t\tduplicate := *input.ExistingBinding\n285|\t\toutcome.Binding = &duplicate\n286|\tcase ActionParked, ActionAttachRemote, ActionTakeoverOffer:\n287|\t\tif !observation.HasWinner {\n288|\t\t\t// No winner establishes no authority: session.parked\n289|\t\t\t// requires a winning lease ID, so the decision\n290|\t\t\t// parks without authoring an event.\n291|\t\t\treturn outcome, nil\n292|\t\t}\n293|\t\tif observation.Winner.HolderHostID != observation.LocalHostID {\n294|\t\t\t// A remote winner holds the lease: the local\n295|\t\t\t// wrapper parks without manufacturing a sequence\n296|\t\t\t// collision under another host's lease (§5.2: the\n297|\t\t\t// winning owner serializes state-changing\n298|\t\t\t// events). No host-local chain record exists for\n299|\t\t\t// a remote park; the decision itself is the\n300|\t\t\t// parked evidence.\n301|\t\t\treturn outcome, nil\n302|\t\t}\n303|\t\tfoldable, err := canAuthorParked(stores.Repo, request.SessionID)\n304|\t\tif err != nil {\n305|\t\t\treturn empty, err\n306|\t\t}\n307|\t\tif !foldable {\n308|\t\t\t// The §5.7 table cannot fold session.parked from\n309|\t\t\t// the derived state: the decision parks without\n310|\t\t\t// authoring an unfolderable lifecycle event.\n311|\t\t\treturn outcome, nil\n312|\t\t}\n313|\t\treference, raw, err := emitParked(stores.Repo, decision, observation, request)\n314|\t\tif err != nil {\n315|\t\t\t// The mutation gate refused (unverified,\n316|\t\t\t// ambiguous, failed handoff, lapsed grant): the\n317|\t\t\t// decision parks without chain evidence rather\n318|\t\t\t// than failing the run. A store failure also\n319|\t\t\t// lands here; unknown is never a launch, but the\n320|\t\t\t// parked decision stands with no event.\n321|\t\t\t// Emit-level refusals are distinguished by the\n322|\t\t\t// fencing owner; repository failures propagate.\n323|\t\t\tif fencing.IsParked(err) || isFencingRefusal(err) {\n324|\t\t\t\treturn outcome, nil\n325|\t\t\t}\n326|\t\t\toutcome.Emitted = false\n327|\t\t\treturn outcome, err\n328|\t\t}\n329|\t\toutcome.Event = &reference\n330|\t\toutcome.EventJSON = raw\n331|\t\toutcome.Emitted = true\n332|\t}\n333|\treturn outcome, nil\n334|}\n335|\n336|// isFencingRefusal reports whether err is a fencing gate refusal\n337|// (as opposed to a repository failure): the parked decision stands\n338|// with no chain evidence when the mutation gate refuses.\n339|func isFencingRefusal(err error) bool {\n340|\tif err == nil {\n341|\t\treturn false\n342|\t}\n343|\tif fencing.IsParked(err) {\n344|\t\treturn true\n345|\t}\n346|\treturn errors.Is(err, fencing.ErrInvalidArguments) ||\n347|\t\terrors.Is(err, fencing.ErrLeaseConflict) ||\n348|\t\terrors.Is(err, fencing.ErrNotOwner) ||\n349|\t\terrors.Is(err, fencing.ErrStaleOwner)\n350|}\n351|\n352|// emitParked authors the parked event under the winning lease the\n353|// local host holds, with the current chain linkage: the next\n354|// sequence under the winning lease, or sequence 1 referencing the\n355|// predecessor head when the winner succeeded the tail lease. The\n356|// presented token is the winning tuple itself, so the mutation\n357|// gate authorizes the locally held winner; the decision's stale or\n358|// unverified presented token never authors.\n359|func emitParked(repository *sessrepo.Repository, decision Decision, observation fencing.Observation, request Request) (sessrepo.EventRef, []byte, error) {\n360|\trecordID, tail, err := ChainTail(repository, request.SessionID)\n361|\tif err != nil {\n362|\t\treturn sessrepo.EventRef{}, nil, err\n363|\t}\n364|\tvar sequence uint64 = 1\n365|\tpredecessors := []string{recordID}\n366|\tif tail != nil {\n367|\t\tif tail.LeaseID == observation.Winner.LeaseID {\n368|\t\t\tsequence = tail.LeaseSequence + 1\n369|\t\t}\n370|\t\tpredecessors = []string{tail.EventID}\n371|\t}\n372|\tpresented := fencing.PresentedToken{\n373|\t\tSessionID: request.SessionID,\n374|\t\tEpoch:     observation.Winner.Epoch,\n375|\t\tLeaseID:   observation.Winner.LeaseID,\n376|\t}\n377|\treturn EmitParked(repository, decision, EmitParams{\n378|\t\tSessionID:     request.SessionID,\n379|\t\tCreatedByHost: request.LocalHostID,\n380|\t\tLeaseEpoch:    observation.Winner.Epoch,\n381|\t\tLeaseID:       observation.Winner.LeaseID,\n382|\t\tLeaseSequence: sequence,\n383|\t\tPredecessors:  predecessors,\n384|\t\tCreatedAt:     request.CreatedAt,\n385|\t\tPresented:     presented,\n386|\t\tObservation:   observation,\n387|\t})\n388|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
