{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cb0d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b131-d4f6-7b82-a7a6-5363cf3ac7fb"},"sequence":993,"recorded_at":1780531400001981,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"2237b1e3-856b-4a22-9f46-61adba667efd","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"2237b1e3-856b-4a22-9f46-61adba667efd","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"2237b1e3-856b-4a22-9f46-61adba667efd"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b136-ee47-74d1-abda-edf7817e7544"},"task_id":"01a0b136-ee47-74d1-abda-edf7817e7544","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b136-ee47-74d1-abda-edf7817e7544","chunk":"Read text file `internal/axpane/doc.go`.\n1|// Package axpane implements the validation core of the\n2|// `ax pane SESSION_ID` enforcement wrapper: the decision every managed\n3|// pane runs before launching, reattaching, offering, parking, or\n4|// refusing a provider.\n5|//\n6|// Normative scope: AX v0.6.0 Section 4.B (Terminal Backend\n7|// Manifest/Probe identity through the landed terminalbackend registry\n8|// and contract), Section 4.C/4.1/4.2 (the wrapper rule: validate\n9|// configuration, load the logical session, synchronize known lease\n10|// records when possible, compare the local fencing token before\n11|// launching a provider, park safely when ownership is remote,\n12|// ambiguous, or unverified; the after-restore sequence 1-5; terminal\n13|// creation and the wrapper's first child start idempotent on\n14|// (session_id, bootstrap_operation_id); no credential-dependent tmux\n15|// server creation from a background caller; a cached sentinel or\n16|// managername observation never authorizes resume), Section 4.D\n17|// (closed capabilities and evidence: only the exact admitted\n18|// capability rows authorize an action), Section 5.2 Terminal Events\n19|// (session.parked with its reason vocabulary, terminal.created and\n20|// session.resumed v4 terminal binding/evidence payloads), Section 7.A\n21|// (Provider Protocol 3.0.0 Terminal Instance binding descriptor),\n22|// and Section 13.1 Direct-session launch steps 3-4 (durable terminal\n23|// entry with the bootstrap operation ID, then provider launch with\n24|// its validated argv/env plan).\n25|//\n26|// Division of authority (composed, not forked): every check is\n27|// composed from a landed gate. Owner epoch and fencing come from\n28|// internal/fencing (AuthorizeActivation, AuthorizeRestore for the\n29|// decision, AuthorizeMutation for every event emission, the sealed\n30|// LeaseToken projection, the parked vocabulary); materialization\n31|// validity from internal/matjournal (Store.Get with its grammar and\n32|// cross-reference validation plus the committed-phase and\n33|// lease-checkpoint-source rules this package states) and checkpoint\n34|// admission from internal/sessckpt (Get, which re-attests) with\n35|// internal/sessrepo attestation (AttestCheckpointRecord) plus the\n36|// winning-lease and session bindings this package states; the\n37|// effective persisted profile from internal/sessprofile\n38|// (DecodeRecord, DecodeEvent, Derive, DeriveForHeads) with Section\n39|// 7.7 mapping refusals from internal/provhost (ResolveMapping,\n40|// profile_mapping_unavailable); provider identity from\n41|// internal/provhost (CheckResumeTuple, VerifyIdentityBuild,\n42|// VerifyIdentityDiscovery) with internal/resumesmoke evidence\n43|// (VerifyRecord) as a precondition input; backend identity from\n44|// internal/terminalbackend (ParseManifest, ParseProbe,\n45|// ParseEvidence, GenerationDigest, Reconcile,\n46|// CapabilitiesForOperation via CheckOperation, CheckEntrypoint,\n47|// AdmitProviderDescriptor); lifecycle foldability from\n48|// internal/sessstate (DecodeRecord, DecodeEvent, Reduce over the\n49|// §5.7 table); configuration validity from internal/config (Load);\n50|// session, lease, and event durability from internal/sessrepo\n51|// (GetRecord, ListEvents, fencing.Observe over ListLeases,\n52|// AppendEvent); refusal shapes from internal/axerror\n53|// (NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable for the background-caller\n54|// capability_unavailable with typed realm/readiness details,\n55|// NewTargetAuthMissing for the smoke precondition).\n56|// ParkedPayload and the evidence-ID pre-checks restate closed-shape\n57|// predicates the canonicaljson owner re-enforces at AppendEvent:\n58|// fail-fast input guards, not a second shape model.\n59|//\n60|// The pure core is Decide: exactly one of\n61|// launch|reattach|attach_remote|takeover_offer|parked(reason)|\n62|// refused(class). Arm order is precedence and is pinned by the\n63|// decision table: configuration, session, bootstrap idempotency\n64|// with the window predicate, backend identity and capability\n65|// admission with the headless conditional, fencing (activation or\n66|// restore entry), materialization with the lease-checkpoint source\n67|// binding, checkpoint bound to the winning lease and session,\n68|// provider identity, provider-auth smoke with the target binding,\n69|// realm evidence, profile derivation from the checkpoint closure on\n70|// resume and mapping, entrypoint, provider descriptor, then the\n71|// outcome selection (reattach on the matching pair, remote\n72|// attach/takeover offer for interactive remote owners, parked in\n73|// all other remote cases, launch).\n74|//\n75|// Durable state: the bootstrap binding store (binding.go) binds\n76|// (session_id, bootstrap_operation_id) to the one recorded\n77|// wrapper/child before any launch side effect under the landed\n78|// no-replace + fsync discipline with crash hooks, superseding\n79|// atomically after the bootstrap window closes. It never persists\n80|// or replicates a PID: identity is the AX-allocated UUIDv7 terminal\n81|// instance ID plus the binding digest. Parked decisions with a\n82|// locally held, verified winner and a foldable lifecycle author\n83|// through sessrepo.AppendEvent under the winning lease (events.go);\n84|// remote, unverifiable, or unfolderable parks carry no chain event\n85|// rather than manufacturing a collision.\n86|//\n87|// Bounds: no `ax` CLI surface, no tmux/ConPTY process control, no\n88|// provider process supervision, no mesh transport, and no GUI/Keychain\n89|// broker live here. Those are modeled callers (their facts arrive as\n90|// Decide inputs) and later leaves. The mesh lease refresh of\n91|// after-restore step 2 is a caller-reported fact (Verified), not a\n92|// network call. Signature verification is caller-supplied through\n93|// terminalbackend.SignatureVerifier.\n94|package axpane","final_result":true}}}
