{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ce51","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b131-d4f6-7b82-a7a6-5363cf3ac7fb"},"sequence":1411,"recorded_at":1780531400002817,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"2237b1e3-856b-4a22-9f46-61adba667efd","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"2237b1e3-856b-4a22-9f46-61adba667efd","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"2237b1e3-856b-4a22-9f46-61adba667efd"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b138-15a6-7812-a325-ca124a9bcea5"},"task_id":"01a0b138-15a6-7812-a325-ca124a9bcea5","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b138-15a6-7812-a325-ca124a9bcea5","chunk":"Read text file `internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n(146 line(s) above)\n147|No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: this package\n148|contains no gate that inspects source text, so the additional\n149|behavioral-suite mutant the evidence contract names for such gates\n150|has no target here. The standalone `CheckResumeTuple` call in\n151|`checkProviderIdentity` is fail-fast ordering over the same gate\n152|`VerifyIdentityBuild` enforces internally, so weakening it alone is\n153|unobservable by construction; likewise the `admitted.Has` realm\n154|pre-check is fail-fast before the evidence cross-bind, so weakening\n155|it alone is unobservable and the binding mutants cover the gate;\n156|the N-identity-version mutant covers the provider-identity gate as\n157|a whole. The fencing entry selection (`AuthorizeRestore` vs\n158|`AuthorizeActivation`) shares one launch-class core in the\n159|`fencing` owner, so no behavioral delta exists to mutate; the\n160|mode-selected backend capability row carries the mode mutant\n161|(N-backend-op).\n162|\n163|## Crash and idempotency evidence\n164|\n165|The bootstrap binding is the only durable write. It installs under\n166|the landed discipline: same-directory staging, 0600, fsync, atomic\n167|link as the no-replace commit, staging cleanup, directory fsync\n168|(skipped, never faked, on Windows). Readers see absence or the\n169|complete receipt, never a torn prefix. Crash hooks arm both\n170|boundaries (`AfterStage` before the commit, `AfterInstall` after\n171|it); the real-kill test (`TestBindCrashChildSelfTerminates`)\n172|SIGKILLs the child between commit and directory sync and proves\n173|the complete binding plus a converging identical retry. Parked\n174|events append through the `sessrepo` owner, whose own crash\n175|evidence stays with that package; this leaf proves linkage and\n176|round-trip only.\n177|\n178|## Stated bounds\n179|\n180|- No `ax` CLI surface, no tmux/ConPTY process control, no provider\n181|  process supervision, no mesh transport, and no GUI/Keychain\n182|  broker live here. Those are modeled callers (their facts arrive\n183|  as `Decide` inputs) and later leaves.\n184|- The bounded mesh lease refresh (after-restore step 2) is the\n185|  caller-reported `Verified` fact, not a network call.\n186|- Signature verification is caller-supplied through\n187|  `terminalbackend.SignatureVerifier`; tests authenticate through\n188|  a generated RSA key.\n189|- Backend liveness (`terminal_backend_unavailable` at the\n190|  operation call site) belongs to the later backend-operation\n191|  leaf: no backend operation exists here, so no availability rule\n192|  is invented.\n193|- The host-local `InstanceBinding` the descriptor must match\n194|  arrives from the modeled backend caller; the wrapper proves\n195|  document-to-binding consistency and never mints backend\n196|  bindings.\n197|- The committed-phase rule for a required materialization is the\n198|  wrapper's stated reading of after-restore step 3 (\"the required\n199|  materialization is valid\").\n200|- Invalid materialization or checkpoint on an otherwise winning\n201|  local owner parks `restore_policy` per the literal step-5\n202|  reading (\"enter parked without launching the provider in all\n203|  other cases\"), with the blocking cause in the decision detail.\n204|- Unknown SESSION_ID refuses `invalid_arguments`: the call names\n205|  no logical session. No `unknown_session` wire code is minted.","final_result":true}}}
