ervations (a union\\ninternal/fencing/gate.go-185-\\t// rival the local store cannot order). Ambiguity parks or refuses.\\ninternal/fencing/gate.go-186-\\tAmbiguous bool\\ninternal/fencing/gate.go-187-\\t// HandoffFailed reports that the caller's own handoff already\\ninternal/fencing/gate.go-188-\\t// failed (a losing force lease before activation). A failed\\ninternal/fencing/gate.go-189-\\t// handoff parks with failed_handoff instead of activating.\\ninternal/fencing/gate.go-190-\\tHandoffFailed bool\\ninternal/fencing/gate.go-191-\\t// Grant is the process-local authorization derived from a winning\\ninternal/fencing/gate.go-192-\\t// lease, meaningful only when HasGrant is set. The gate re-checks\\ninternal/fencing/gate.go-193-\\t// its expiry through the sessrepo owner on every call.\\ninternal/fencing/gate.go-194-\\tGrant    sessrepo.FencingGrant\\ninternal/fencing/gate.go-195-\\tHasGrant bool\\ninternal/fencing/gate.go-196-\\t// Policy carries the configured lease refresh interval the\\ninternal/fencing/gate.go-197-\\t// expiry arm enforces.\\ninternal/fencing/gate.go-198-\\tPolicy sessrepo.FencingPolicy\\ninternal/fencing/gate.go-199-\\t// Now is the caller's clock reading for the expiry arm. A grant\\ninternal/fencing/gate.go-200-\\t// without a clock reading refuses rather than bypassing expiry.\\ninternal/fencing/gate.go-201-\\tNow time.Time\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go:142:type LeaseSummary struct {\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-143-\\tRecordID       string\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-144-\\tSessionID      string\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-145-\\tLeaseID        string\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-146-\\tEpoch          uint64\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-147-\\tHolderHostID   string\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-148-\\tPredecessor    string\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-149-\\tHasPredecessor bool\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-150-\\tCheckpoint     string\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-151-\\tHasCheckpoint  bool\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-152-\\tReason         string\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-153-}\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-154-\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-155-// FencingToken is a presented ownership proof: the epoch, lease ID, and\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-156-// holder the presenter claims.\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-157-type FencingToken struct {\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-158-\\tEpoch        uint64\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-159-\\tLeaseID      string\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-160-\\tHolderHostID string\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-161-}\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-162-\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3540,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 885,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
