{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e54b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b131-d4f6-7b82-a7a6-5363cf3ac7fb"},"sequence":4352,"recorded_at":1780531400008699,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"2237b1e3-856b-4a22-9f46-61adba667efd","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"2237b1e3-856b-4a22-9f46-61adba667efd","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"2237b1e3-856b-4a22-9f46-61adba667efd"},"call_id":"call_01a0b14e2a5e729fbc6d92e032b1881f","text":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(2149 line(s) above)\n2150|## Pane enforcement wrapper (`ax pane` validation core)\n2151|\n2152|[`internal/axpane`](internal/axpane) implements the validation core of the\n2153|`ax pane SESSION_ID` enforcement wrapper: the decision every managed pane runs\n2154|before launching, reattaching, offering, parking, or refusing a provider\n2155|(pinned Sections 4.B-4.D, 4.1-4.2, 5.2 Terminal Events, 7.A, and 13.1, plus the\n2156|2.4 profile authority). The pure core `Decide` returns exactly one of\n2157|`launch`, `reattach`, `attach_remote`, `takeover_offer`, `parked(reason)`, or\n2158|`refused(class)`, composing every check from a landed gate: owner epoch and\n2159|fencing from `fencing` (activation or restore entry, sealed `LeaseToken`,\n2160|parked vocabulary), materialization from `matjournal` plus checkpoint admission\n2161|from `sessckpt`/`sessrepo`, the effective profile from `sessprofile` with\n2162|`provhost` mapping refusals, provider identity from `provhost` with\n2163|`resumesmoke` evidence as a precondition, backend identity and closed\n2164|capabilities from `terminalbackend`, configuration from `config`, and refusal\n2165|shapes from `axerror`, and lifecycle foldability from `sessstate`. `Run`\n2166|orchestrates the adapters over the durable stores and applies exactly the\n2167|authorized effect: launch binds the bootstrap `(session_id,\n2168|bootstrap_operation_id)` pair before any provider side effect (superseding\n2169|atomically after the window closes), reattach returns the one recorded child,\n2170|verified locally held foldable parks author `session.parked` under the winning\n2171|lease through the `AuthorizeMutation` gate, remote/unverifiable/unfolderable\n2172|parks author no chain event, and refused decisions write nothing. The bootstrap\n2173|store installs under the no-replace plus fsync discipline with crash hooks,\n2174|persists no PID, reattaches linearizably on the commit race, and sweeps stale\n2175|pre-commit staging; a background caller authorizes only through the admitted\n2176|`credential_capable_execution_realm` row bound to the host binding, probed\n2177|build, and current generation, refusing `capability_unavailable` with typed\n2178|realm/readiness details otherwise, and no cached sentinel, `managername`\n2179|observation, or bare boolean can authorize resume. Resume derives the\n2180|effective profile from the validated checkpoint's event-head closure, and a\n2181|non-interactive create requires `headless_creation`.\n2182|\n2183|Run the focused tests and coverage with:\n2184|\n2185|```bash\n2186|go test ./internal/axpane -count=1\n2187|go test ./internal/axpane -cover -count=1\n2188|```\n2189|\n2190|Run the narrowing battery (35 narrowing mutants plus one harmless control)\n2191|with:\n2192|\n2193|```bash\n2194|PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/axpane/mutant_harness.py\n2195|```\n2196|\n2197|The harness mutates one production file in place, runs the named killer\n2198|through the production entry point, restores the file from backup, and reports\n2199|per-row verdicts with subprocess exits; `AX_MUTANT_VERBOSE=1` additionally\n2200|prints the raw per-plant logs. Task validation logs and mutation artifacts are\n2201|attached to `TASK-260830-1geqhj`. The package adds no `ax` command, no\n2202|`doctor` result, and no runtime capability claim; the clause-to-test matrix\n2203|with its stated bounds lives in\n2204|[the task evidence map](internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md).\n2205|\n2206|\n2207|## Ownership reducer properties\n2208|\n2209|The four story-pinned ownership invariants (pinned v0.6.0 Sections 2.2, 5.3,\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
